    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
    <tr>
        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <p><b>Bug Type:</b> Functional / Room Activation / Gameplay Exploit</p>

<p><b>Priority:</b> Medium</p>

<p><b>Preconditions:</b></p>

<ul>
	<li>Game is running and the player is exploring a dungeon.</li>
	<li>The selected character is Doraemon.</li>
	<li>The player approaches a combat room containing multiple enemies.</li>
	<li>The combat room has not been cleared or activated.</li>
	<li>The room entrance is accessible.</li>
</ul>


<p><b>Steps to Reproduce:</b></p>

<ol>
	<li>Start the game and select Doraemon.</li>
	<li>Find a combat room containing enemies.</li>
	<li>Enter the room through an open doorway.</li>
	<li>Instead of moving toward the center, stay close to the walls and move along the room's perimeter.</li>
	<li>Continue moving around the edges of the room, including areas close to enemies.</li>
	<li>Observe the enemies' movement, attack behavior, and the room's gate status.</li>
	<li>Move farther into the interior of the room.</li>
	<li>Observe whether the gates close and the enemies become active.</li>
</ol>


<p><b>Expected Result:</b></p>

<ul>
	<li>Once the player has entered the intended combat area, the room should activate correctly.</li>
	<li>The gates should close to prevent the player from leaving before defeating the enemies (TC-RM-01).</li>
	<li>Enemies should become active and respond to the player's presence after the encounter is triggered.</li>
	<li>The player should not be able to freely explore a substantial portion of an uncleared combat room without triggering the encounter.</li>
	<li>The activation boundary should be consistent with the room's visible entrance and playable area.</li>
</ul>


<p><b>Actual Result:</b></p>

<ul>
	<li>Doraemon can enter the combat room and move along its perimeter without immediately activating the encounter.</li>
	<li>Enemies remain stationary and do not chase or attack the player, even when Doraemon moves close to them.</li>
	<li>The room gates remain open while the player follows the perimeter.</li>
	<li>The player's HP and armor remain unchanged during the observed movement.</li>
	<li>The enemies only become active after Doraemon moves farther into the room.</li>
	<li>At approximately 11 seconds in the recording, the message "GATES SEALED — VANQUISH THE HORDE!" appears, indicating that the room has finally been activated.</li>
</ul>


<p><b>Test Case Result:</b></p>

<ul>
	<li><b>FAIL — Potential room activation boundary issue</b></li>
	<li><b>Related Test Cases:</b>
	<ul>
		<li>TC-RM-01: Combat room gates close when the encounter is triggered.</li>
		<li>TC-RM-05: Enemies become active after the room is locked.</li>
		<li>TC-RM-03: The player cannot leave an active, locked combat room.</li>
	</ul>
	</li>
	<li><b>Regression Testing:</b> Required after confirmation and correction of the activation rules.</li>
</ul>


<p><b>Notes:</b></p>

<ul>
	<li>Source code inspection suggests that this behavior may be caused by the combat room's activation condition rather than an enemy AI malfunction.</li>
	<li>In <tt>room_manager.gd</tt>, the <tt>_is_player_deep_inside_room()</tt> function checks whether the player's position is inside an inset area of the room (<tt>room_rect.grow(-1)</tt>).</li>
	<li>If the player stays near the room boundary without entering this activation area, the room may remain unlocked and its enemies inactive.</li>
	<li>This depth requirement appears intentional, but the current activation boundary may allow the player to move too far inside the visible combat room without triggering the encounter.</li>
	<li>Verify whether this behavior is intended by the level design.</li>
	<li>Check whether players can bypass combat rooms entirely by following the perimeter.</li>
	<li>Check whether enemies can be attacked or defeated before the room is activated.</li>
	<li>Test the behavior at all room entrances and along every wall.</li>
	<li>Repeat the test using other playable characters.</li>
	<li>Verify that the room activates consistently when the player crosses its intended trigger boundary.</li>
	<li>If the player can bypass mandatory combat encounters, consider increasing the priority to <b>High</b>.</li>
</ul>


<p><b>Relevant Source Files:</b></p>

<ul>
	<li><tt>Scene/Map/room_manager.gd</tt></li>
	<li><tt>Scene/Map/DungeonSpawner.gd</tt></li>
	<li><tt>Scene/Map/RoomManager.tscn</tt></li>
</ul>


<p><b>Attachment:</b></p>

<ul>
	<li><tt>Screen Recording 2026-11-18 220315.mp4</tt></li>
</ul>


<p><b>Status:</b> To Do</p>
